# Source key: projects:masters_guide_welcome_title
projects-masters_guide_welcome_title = Meet your Zapper

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_welcome_body
projects-masters_guide_welcome_body = A Zapper turns one brief into coordinated work. It plans, hands tasks to separate chats called slaves, and follows up on them.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_welcome_preview
projects-masters_guide_welcome_preview = Preview: your Zapper and its slaves run on the computer it was created on, so keep it on and connected.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_repositories_title
projects-masters_guide_repositories_title = Choose repositories

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_repositories_summary
projects-masters_guide_repositories_summary = Decide where your Zapper may work.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_repositories_body
projects-masters_guide_repositories_body = Your Zapper only works in the repositories you add here. Adding one doesn’t send its existing chats anything.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_repositories_empty
projects-masters_guide_repositories_empty = None yet? Open a repository in Zuse first, then add it here.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_repositories_optional
projects-masters_guide_repositories_optional = You can change these at any time.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_brief_title
projects-masters_guide_brief_title = Write a brief

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_brief_summary
projects-masters_guide_brief_summary = Describe the outcome you want.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_brief_body
projects-masters_guide_brief_body = Say what done looks like: the outcome, the scope and any constraints. Your Zapper plans and delegates from there.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_brief_model
projects-masters_guide_brief_model = The model picker sets the model your Zapper plans with. Standing instructions live in Preferences.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_brief_example
projects-masters_guide_brief_example = Try an example

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_brief_example_hint
projects-masters_guide_brief_example_hint = Adds editable text. Nothing is sent.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_example_delegate
projects-masters_guide_example_delegate = Plan and delegate

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_example_delegate_text
projects-masters_guide_example_delegate_text = Review this repository, propose a plan, then delegate independent fixes to separate chats. Ask me before changing scope or merging.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_example_tests
projects-masters_guide_example_tests = Fix failing tests

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_example_tests_text
projects-masters_guide_example_tests_text = Find the failing tests, group them by cause, and fix each group in a separate chat. Summarize what changed when you’re done.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_example_reviews
projects-masters_guide_example_reviews = Unblock pull requests

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_example_reviews_text
projects-masters_guide_example_reviews_text = Go through the open pull requests, list what blocks each one, and fix the simple blockers in separate chats. Ask me before merging.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_slaves_title
projects-masters_guide_slaves_title = Follow its slaves

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_slaves_summary
projects-masters_guide_slaves_summary = Check on and steer each task.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_slaves_body
projects-masters_guide_slaves_body = Each slave is a separate chat doing one task. Open one to see progress, steer it or answer permission requests.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_slaves_controls
projects-masters_guide_slaves_controls = Pause stops new work from being handed out. Stop also interrupts work that’s running.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_continuity_title
projects-masters_guide_continuity_title = Start fresh, keep context

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_continuity_summary
projects-masters_guide_continuity_summary = Begin a new chat without losing track.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_continuity_body
projects-masters_guide_continuity_body = When a conversation gets long, choose Fresh chat here. Repositories, running slaves, decisions and memory carry over.

# Source key: projects:masters_guide_continuity_memory
projects-masters_guide_continuity_memory = Replay this guide from this menu at any time.

# Source key: projects:masters_paused_notice
projects-masters_paused_notice = Paused. Your Zapper can reply, but won’t start or message slaves until you resume.

# Source key: projects:masters_stopped_notice
projects-masters_stopped_notice = Stopped. Your Zapper can reply, but won’t start or message slaves until you resume.

